WEBVTT

00:46:29.917 --> 00:46:32.934
your concepts of give and take,
your concept of asking for help

00:46:32.958 --> 00:46:37.143
of what you can ask from whom,
et cetera, expectations.

00:46:37.167 --> 00:46:39.309
And the loyalty thing is, you know,

00:46:39.333 --> 00:46:41.768
the messages really say
you're never alone,

00:46:41.792 --> 00:46:43.851
you owe a lot of things
to a lot of people,

00:46:43.875 --> 00:46:46.393
and a lot of people are there for you.

00:46:46.417 --> 00:46:48.893
In my thinking, when I have a problem,

00:46:48.917 --> 00:46:51.351
the first thing I think
is who can help me?

00:46:51.375 --> 00:46:52.893
I don't think, "What can I do?"

00:46:52.917 --> 00:46:54.268
I think, "Who can help me?"

00:46:54.292 --> 00:46:57.268
Because there's people
who know more than me about this thing

00:46:57.292 --> 00:46:58.934
and will help me think it through.

00:46:58.958 --> 00:47:03.184
And I in American parlance
can be seen as someone who pulls.